---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { labs } from '../lib/labs.mjs';
import { contactEmail } from '../lib/env';
---
<Layout
  title="About Classroom Labs: Free Learning Sites for Class"
  description="Classroom Labs is the home of eight free, interactive learning sites for science, math, coding and reading, made by one independent maker for classrooms."
  crumbs={[['About']]}
  nav="About"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-intro">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <span aria-current="page">About</span></nav>
      <h1>About Classroom Labs</h1>
      <p class="lede">Classroom Labs is the home of a family of free, interactive learning sites, each one built around a subject taught in school.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What the labs are</h2>
      <p>Each lab is its own website with simulations, calculators, games and practice that run in the browser. Students change something and see what happens: an orbit, a Punnett square, a river, a triangle, a sentence. There are eight so far:</p>
      <ul>
        {labs.map(lab => <li><a href={lab.url} data-lab={lab.id}>{lab.name}</a> ({lab.subject.toLowerCase()})</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h2>How they are made</h2>
      <p>The labs are made for classrooms. They are free to use with no sign-up, so a teacher can share a link and students can start straight away, on a Chromebook or any other device with a browser. The science, math and reading labs come with printable activities and answer keys for teachers.</p>
      <p>Every lab stays free for students. Alongside that, a paid <a href="/#teacher-plan">teacher plan</a> for teachers and schools is being planned, with extras for running a class. Teachers on the waitlist will be asked what it should include.</p>

      <h2>Who makes it</h2>
      <p>Classroom Labs is made by one independent maker, not a publisher or a large company. It started with Interactive Periodic Table and has grown one subject at a time.</p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>Questions, corrections and ideas from teachers are welcome. {contactEmail ? <Fragment>Write to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.</Fragment> : <Fragment>See the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</Fragment>}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
